# requirements.md Content

```md
# Requirements

## Functional Requirements
1. Create bank account
2. Deposit money
3. Withdraw money
4. Check balance
5. Store records using file handling

## Non-Functional Requirements
- User-friendly
- Secure
- Reliable

## Hardware Requirements
- Intel i3 or above
- 2GB RAM

## Software Requirements
- C++
- GCC Compiler
Steps to Upload to GitHub
1. Create Repository

Go to:

GitHub

Click:

New Repository
Repository Name → Bank-Management-System
Click Create Repository
2. Open Terminal in Project Folder

Example:

cd Bank-Management-System
3. Initialize Git
git init
4. Add Files
git add .
5. Commit Files
git commit -m "Initial commit"
6. Connect GitHub Repository

Replace yourusername with your GitHub username.

git remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/Bank-Management-System.git
7. Push to GitHub
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
Files You Should Upload
bank.cpp
README.md
requirements.md
Bank_Management_Application_Report.pdf

Do not upload bank.dat if it contains real customer data.
